The Warp Agent CLI (the `warp` command) installed through asdf.

Warp ships prebuilt, versioned, per-architecture tarballs on Google Cloud
Storage. This plugin resolves the right artifact for your host, downloads it,
verifies it against the digest Google publishes, and unpacks it.

Supported hosts:
  macOS  arm64  ->  warp-tui-<channel>-macos-aarch64.tar.gz
  macOS  x64    ->  warp-tui-<channel>-macos-x86_64.tar.gz
  Linux  arm64  ->  warp-tui-<channel>-linux-aarch64.tar.gz
  Linux  x64    ->  warp-tui-<channel>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz

Commands:
  asdf list warp              list installed versions
  asdf list-all warp          list every published version
  asdf install warp latest    install the current stable build
  asdf global warp <version>  pin the version for every shell
  asdf reshim warp            refresh the `warp` shim

The CLI is the same agent you get in the Warp desktop app, running in any
terminal. It needs a Warp account: run `warp` once and follow the login link.
